{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I fell in my bathroom about four weeks ago. My left knee gave out. I went to the hospital then, but they said the CT was normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And what changed recently?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I woke up two days ago with sharp pain in my right hip. I couldn’t walk at all. That’s when I came here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We did an MRI tonight, and it shows a small fracture in your right hip bone—specifically the acetabulum. It’s not displaced, so surgery isn’t needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A fracture? But the CT was normal weeks ago. How come?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes small fractures don’t show up on CT right away. The MRI is more sensitive. This one looks subacute—meaning it’s been there a while but got worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So what now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll manage it without surgery. You’ll need to limit weight-bearing and start physical therapy. Ortho reviewed your case and agreed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to walk again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with time and rehab. You’re already using a walker, which helps. We’ll make sure you have home therapy after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s good. My hip hurts a lot, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The MRI also found something else—a possible tear in one of the muscles near your hip, the gluteus medius. That could be making the pain worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A muscle tear? From the fall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. It might have started then and worsened over time, especially if you’ve been limping. We’ll manage the pain with medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my other medicines? I take a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we reviewed them. You’re on tacrolimus for your kidney transplant. Your level was a bit low—2.7, which is below the target."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not immediately. The transplant team recommended increasing your dose from 3 mg to 4 mg twice daily to keep your levels stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my kidney numbers?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is 2.2, which is consistent with your baseline Stage IV CKD. No acute kidney injury. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I remember last time my levels went up and I got confused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be careful. Your blood pressure is a bit high today—138/90. We’ll continue your amlodipine, furosemide, and now add chlorthalidone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I also take omeprazole for my reflux. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2161-04-14 21:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep that. And your sodium bicarbonate for the low bicarbonate level—your body’s slightly acidic, but stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2161-04-15 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We did an X-ray yesterday. It didn’t show the fracture—sometimes X-rays miss small ones—but it confirms no new changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2161-04-15 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the MRI was right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2161-04-15 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. MRI is better for spotting early or subtle fractures. We’re confident in the diagnosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2161-04-15 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the muscle tear? Can that heal without surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2161-04-15 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. For now, rest and physical therapy will help. Surgery isn’t urgent. We’ll follow up with ortho after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs today look stable. Hemoglobin is 8.1—still a bit low, but not dropping. We won’t need a transfusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel tired. Is that from the anemia?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. Also, healing takes energy. We’ll keep supporting you with nutrition and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My pain is better with the oxycodone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2161-04-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep it as needed. Just watch for drowsiness, especially with your other meds like clonazepam."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2161-04-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re making progress. PT saw you yesterday and says you’re starting to bear some weight with the walker."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2161-04-17 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s still painful, but I can move a little more each time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2161-04-17 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s exactly what we want to see. Healing takes time, but you’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2161-04-17 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need the enoxaparin you started?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2161-04-17 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, for two weeks. Since you’re not moving much, it helps prevent blood clots. It’s a low dose, safe with your kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2161-04-18 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your tacrolimus level came back this morning—3.6. That’s much better, now in the target range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2161-04-18 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the dose increase is working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2161-04-18 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Keep taking it as prescribed. Your nephrologist will check it weekly for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2161-04-18 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure? It’s been high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2161-04-18 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re managing it. Today it’s 158/80, which is a bit up, but we’ve added chlorthalidone. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today. You’ll have a visiting nurse for physical therapy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most stay the same. Key changes: tacrolimus is now 4 mg twice daily, and you’ll take enoxaparin daily for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And pain medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Oxycodone as needed, but try acetaminophen first. Call if pain worsens or you have swelling, fever, or trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep your follow-ups with nephrology, ortho, and your primary doctor. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to go. I just want to get stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2161-04-19 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you will. Take it one day at a time. We’ll see you in clinic soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2161-04-14 21:22:00",
    "admission_end": "2161-04-19 18:43:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted following a fall four weeks prior, initially with mild hip pain, but presented acutely with inability to ambulate due to worsening right hip pain. MRI revealed a non-displaced right acetabular fracture and a possible gluteus medius rupture, both managed non-operatively. She was treated with pain control using oxycodone and acetaminophen, and physical therapy was initiated. Her chronic kidney disease remained stable, and transplant nephrology adjusted her tacrolimus dose from 3 mg to 4 mg twice daily due to subtherapeutic levels, with subsequent improvement in drug levels. Hypertension was managed with continuation of amlodipine, furosemide, and addition of chlorthalidone. She was discharged home with home physical therapy, enoxaparin for thromboprophylaxis, and close outpatient follow-up for nephrology and orthopedic monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Closed fracture of acetabulum",
      "Chronic kidney disease, Stage IV (severe)",
      "Late effects of cerebrovascular disease, hemiplegia affecting unspecified side",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
